{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:1-3", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1-3"}, "paraphrase": "The brāhmaṇa Triśikhi goes to Āditya's world and asks what the body is, what the life-breath, what the cause and what the Self; the Sun answers: all is Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:trisikhi", "tch:aditya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:103-105", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "103-105"}, "paraphrase": "Prāṇāyāma has three grades: the lowest produces sweat, the middle trembling, the highest rising of the body.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:119-127", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "119-127"}, "paraphrase": "Omens of death: when throbbing ceases in certain places of the limbs the remaining life is a year, six months, three months and so on; not seeing the tip of one's tongue, a few days.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:death-omens"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:128-133", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "128-133"}, "paraphrase": "Pratyāhāra: holding the breath successively at eighteen vital points (marma) of the body, from the toes upward, and back.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:marmasthana-dharana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:134-143", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "134-143"}, "paraphrase": "Element-concentrations with the vyūha deities: earth with Aniruddha, water with Nārāyaṇa, fire with Pradyumna, air with Saṅkarṣaṇa, space with Vāsudeva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:element-dharanas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:148-151", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "148-151"}, "paraphrase": "The states are placed in the body: waking between navel and heart, dream in the throat, deep sleep in the palate, the fourth between the brows, the beyond-fourth in the brahmarandhra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:160-161", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "160-161"}, "paraphrase": "Samādhi is the knowledge 'I am the supreme Brahman'; the yogin becomes Brahman.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:19-27", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "19-27"}, "paraphrase": "From yoga comes knowledge and from knowledge yoga; yoga is twofold — of knowledge and of action; the yogin established in both never perishes.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:yoga-jnana-samuccaya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:28-31", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "28-31"}, "paraphrase": "In the yoga of knowledge the limbs are redefined: yama is dispassion toward body and senses; niyama constant attachment to the supreme; āsana indifference to all things; prāṇāyāma knowing the world as unreal; pratyāhāra turning the mind inward; dhāraṇā motionless mind; dhyāna 'I am pure consciousness'; samādhi the forgetting of meditation.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:jnana-limbs"], "paths": ["pth:trisikhi-eight-limbs"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:32-33", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "32-33"}, "paraphrase": "Ten yamas — non-injury, truth, non-stealing, celibacy, compassion, rectitude, forbearance, fortitude, moderate diet, purity; ten niyamas — austerity, contentment, faith, charity, worship of Hari, hearing Vedānta, modesty, discernment (mati), japa, vows.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-yamas-ten-niyamas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:34-52", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "34-52"}, "paraphrase": "Seventeen postures are described — svastika, gomukha, vīra, yoga, padma, baddhapadma, kukkuṭa, uttāna-kūrma, dhanur, siṃha, bhadra, mukta, mayūra, matsya, siddha, paścimatāna and sukha; conquering posture conquers the three worlds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:asanas-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:54-75", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "54-75"}, "paraphrase": "The body is ninety-six digits; the fire-centre has a different shape in each species; at the navel is a twelve-spoked wheel ('I turn it by my māyā'), where the jīva moves like a spider in its web; kuṇḍalī lies coiled eightfold; the channels spread from the kanda.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis", "cpt:kundalini"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad:76-86", "source": "src:trisikhibrahmana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "76-86"}, "paraphrase": "The ten vital winds and their functions: prāṇa, apāna, samāna, udāna, vyāna; nāga for belching, kūrma for blinking, kṛkara for sneezing and hunger, devadatta for sleep and yawning, dhanañjaya which does not leave even the corpse.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-vayus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
